{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals","id":1007970,"title":"Is Brawl useless for mortals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-24T23:55:51-08:00","id":1007970,"title":"Is Brawl useless for mortals?","content":"So most of my players have about 6 defence and one has some decent brawl but found that if I give npcs that type of defence then the brawler of the group is running on a luck die to do anything physical.<br /> <br /> So it kinda feels useless to even put points into strength and brawl at low levels.<br /> <br /> Would it be too game breaking to roll brawl with strength and dex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T00:04:54-08:00","id":1007973,"title":"","content":"Make them use knuckle-duster - <i>any</i> weapon in 2E <b>CoD</b> makes Lethal damage. Even with bonus 0L, any damage would be serious threat to other mortal characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T00:43:45-08:00","id":1007980,"title":"","content":"Brawl is good because it can grapple. It's probably best &quot;one on one&quot; tactic, because if you are skilled grappler, and they aren't, you basically shut them down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T01:23:23-08:00","id":1007987,"title":"","content":"Brawl isn't useless (it's not like Weaponry gets better rolls to hit either, even if it gets better damage output), but it is the least effective combat focused Skill for mortals in terms of raw combat optimization.<br /> <br /> Some of that is on purpose: the CofD takes place in a world similar to our own, and you expect a sword to beat fists, and a gun to beat either, everything else being equal.<br /> <br /> Some of it is also that the CofD is a supernatural setting, and the supernaturals with big boosts to Brawl are kind of crazily nasty with it, so any boosts to make Brawl better risks making it overpowered once in supernatural hands.<br /> <br /> So, without same major house ruling, brawlers do best to concentrate on their strongest option: All out Attack + WP to initiate grapples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T02:12:03-08:00","id":1007997,"title":"","content":"Yeah, basically sword beats fists any time you might face more than one opponent, fist beats sword and gun anytime you are facing one opponent, and gun is easiest to use but also most vulnerable to cover and things like that - low weapon rating guns can be fully stopped by cover quite reliably, as you need your weapon rating to exceed cover rating in order to do any damage at all. And that's actually a challenge with &quot;typical&quot; street guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T04:51:56-08:00","id":1008028,"title":"","content":"Brawl requires the most investment to be e effective. Guns require the least. Guns are the best against large numbers of targets. Brawl is the best one on one.<br /> <br /> The thing to consider about brawl is that every serious combatant needs to purchase an answer to being grappled. The only built in answer is allies.<br /> <br /> Weapon Crafting also messes withthis system a lot. When anyone can have a 4L Chains and 4L Brass Knuckles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:37:22-08:00","id":1008037,"title":"","content":"A character isn't always going to have a weapon. So brawl will never be <i>useless</i> for a mortal, even if having it as their preferred form of combat requires a bit of investment, like the fighting merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:11:35-08:00","id":1008047,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies. It seems like grappling is the best way and having another to attack so they don't have defence and having knuckle dusters to make any success lethal. <br /> <br /> It just seems to be wasteful for hunter mortals to buy certain unarmed fighting merits to go against just thugs or cultists (from hurt locker too) but thinking about it the suggestion I had would just make brawl too strong over weapons. <br /> <br /> Also while Im here:<br /> <br /> In hurt locker whats the rules for defence against bow and arrows? Is it full defence or no defence? I just used no defence for a player using one as I couldnt remember and he was using firearms. <br /> <br /> I'm just wondering to go half way with defence like half it down as it feels like you could dodge an arrow but only just.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:50:28-08:00","id":1008082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutedMirth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008047#post1008047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In hurt locker whats the rules for defence against bow and arrows? Is it full defence or no defence? I just used no defence for a player using one as I couldnt remember and he was using firearms.<br /> <br /> I'm just wondering to go half way with defence like half it down as it feels like you could dodge an arrow but only just.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arrows are rather annoying here. They exist in a problematic speed slot. Normal humans can't react to arrows, but it IS possible for highly trained people to get to that level.<br /> I dunno how to fix that tbh. Overall I'd say &quot;no defence against arrows&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:59:32-08:00","id":1008088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008082#post1008082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arrows are rather annoying here. They exist in a problematic speed slot. Normal humans can't react to arrows, but it IS possible for highly trained people to get to that level.<br /> I dunno how to fix that tbh. Overall I'd say &amp;quot;no defence against arrows&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like something to make a Merit for. Otherwise, I'd just use the rules for defense against firearms. No defense beyond close range, defense capped by the weapon's size at close range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:14:24-08:00","id":1008166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008088#post1008088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like something to make a Merit for. Otherwise, I'd just use the rules for defense against firearms. No defense beyond close range, defense capped by the weapon's size at close range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah thats what I settled for but wasn't sure as arrows are fast so couldn't imagine someone dodging one without supernatual reflexes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:19:32-08:00","id":1008169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutedMirth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008166#post1008166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah thats what I settled for but wasn't sure as arrows are fast so couldn't imagine someone dodging one without supernatual reflexes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, close range it's less about dodging the arrow and more about being a difficult target for the archer to get a bead on. Beyond that, yeah, you're not going to be able to dodge it short of supernatural reflexes, or highly specialized training.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T12:22:09-08:00","id":1008235,"title":"","content":"Bows are actually garbage at short range IRL - it might be OK to just make it so you can't use them to attack people within short range <i>at all</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:56:21-08:00","id":1008259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008235#post1008235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bows are actually garbage at short range IRL - it might be OK to just make it so you can't use them to attack people within short range <i>at all</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes sense. In the Hurt Locker previews, bows are a Medium range weapon without a Merit. It would make a lot of sense to bump that up to Long (Extreme with the Merit) and say the target gets the bow'/ Size to Defense at Short, and they can't be used at Close at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:47:51-08:00","id":1008278,"title":"","content":"I might be totally off, but isn't Defense-Against-Firearms pretty rare in 2nd Edition now? I think I remember that in 1st edition, it was super easy to get your supernatural paws on it; my inaccurate recall of 2nd ed is that supernatural usually don't get it for free, and even then, it's either &quot;add dots in this power to 0 and use that as your Defence&quot;, or &quot;in this murderface warform, go nuts, full defense&quot;? If so, it makes firearms The Great Equalizer for mortals, in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:55:25-08:00","id":1008282,"title":"","content":"Vampires can use Celerity or an Auspex + Celerity devotion.<br /> <br /> Werewolves get normal defense against firearms in most non-hishu forms.<br /> <br /> Changelings require a specific Kith to do it. They can get psuedo defense via several contracts, or just be straight immune to physical damage.<br /> <br /> Mage I don't know offhand.<br /> <br /> Demons can't, but otoh they really don't need to. They have other, very powerful, defenses.<br /> <br /> Beasts can't easily do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:49:21-08:00","id":1008300,"title":"","content":"A few Mage Armors give Defense equal to the relevant Arcana against Firearms, if I recall correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:02:02-08:00","id":1008306,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that 6 defense is quite high for regular mortal antagonists. Your average person on the street probably has 3, and even a regular bouncer type probably shouldn't have more than 5. Unless the opponents are supposed to be people with above average aptitude and combat training I would just lower their dots in the relevant traits by 1 or 2. <br /> <br /> You can also make combat faster and more exciting by having the enemies All Out Attack more often. The dice bonus it gives is usually a pretty poor trade for lost defense, so while the PCs will be seeing more damage come their way they also have a *much* better shot at hitting back.<br /> <br /> As for supernaturals and bullets, you run into an issue where they don't really even need defense because armor powers are so common and can reduce smaller guns to little more than annoyances. When your ranged weapons mostly have small flat bonuses (outside shotguns and large rifles) and your supernatural melee weapons often scale, melee becomes king.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:48:53-08:00","id":1008365,"title":"","content":"I've yet to see a decent argument for why Brawl and Weaponry aren't just a Melee skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:16:17-08:00","id":1008374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008365#post1008365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've yet to see a decent argument for why Brawl and Weaponry aren't just a Melee skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the real answer is probably so that each category has the same number of Skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T20:06:58-08:00","id":1008388,"title":"","content":"It's mechanically and thematically different. Can't grapple with Weaponry. Weaponry, generally, does Lethal on its own as opposed to Brawl which for the most part does Bashing. One can walk through the streets with hands and feet without gaining much attention as opposed to most Weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T20:22:30-08:00","id":1008392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008388#post1008388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mechanically and thematically different. Can't grapple with Weaponry. Weaponry, generally, does Lethal on its own as opposed to Brawl which for the most part does Bashing. One can walk through the streets with hands and feet without gaining much attention as opposed to most Weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but theoretically, you could just use specialties to cover the difference since the gulf between Brawl and Weaponry is relatively tiny since learning parts of one can influence learning with the other.<br /> <br /> I mean, Science, Academics, and Crafts are all one skill when they could theoretically be split up into more.<br /> <br /> Granted, I suppose the lack of a good replacement skill is a good reason not to merge them together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T21:10:35-08:00","id":1008403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008392#post1008392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but theoretically, you could just use specialties to cover the difference since the gulf between Brawl and Weaponry is relatively tiny since learning parts of one can influence learning with the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a tiny difference. Look where your hands are. With weaponry, you're aiming at least a foot away from them.<br /> <br /> Certainly there's a lot of athleticism in both, but the moves and actions aren't the same. They aren't even the same in themselves. A staff fighter is going to fight differently than a sword fighter just like a boxer is going to fight differently from a judo master.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, Science, Academics, and Crafts are all one skill when they could theoretically be split up into more. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's like the differences here. Science can allow you to appreciate how to build things, but doesn't necessarily let you build things and on its own has a lot more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T00:30:27-08:00","id":1008448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008374#post1008374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the real answer is probably so that each category has the same number of Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't impossible to address though.<br /> <br /> First thing that comes to mind is breaking up Expression to get Performance as a physical Skill. Expression focuses on the production and delivery of words and images, while Performance focuses on the physical motions used to artistically communicate ideas. Separating out oratory and journalism, from dancing and doing stunt work doesn't seem like it would be a problem for anyone; maybe even siphon a bit off of Athletics since it's one of the broader Skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008388#post1008388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mechanically and thematically different. Can't grapple with Weaponry. Weaponry, generally, does Lethal on its own as opposed to Brawl which for the most part does Bashing. One can walk through the streets with hands and feet without gaining much attention as opposed to most Weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>How mechanically different are they?<br /> <br /> They both operate at the same range, and deal with the same general situational issues. Both can deal Bashing or Lethal if you invest in the right options. Both can even impact grapples. Not all Weaponry options are equally likely to attract attention.<br /> <br /> So it seems like the mechanical difference is fairly small. A lot of it has more to do with things like how they interact with Merits; which could be maintained fairly easily.<br /> <br /> Is the thematic difference important to CofD?<br /> <br /> There are plenty of games were the Brawler and the Swordsman are valuable as thematically different archetypes that they deserve significant representation. Why is it important to break up close-combat fighting into these in the CofD? The vast majority of people that are trained to fight in real world circumstances are trained to fight armed and unarmed. And this has been true for most of history. The thematic appeal to genre doesn't seem to have a lot of place in the CofD. Horror/Urban Fantasy doesn't put much stress on these things (and it can be done when needed with things like Kiths from Changeling where these narrative archetypes matter significantly). The idea that your average street thug needs different Skills for beating you with a baseball bat or kicking your ribs in doesn't seem to bare out. Playing a beat cop or someone that did a tour in Iraq makes having Brawl and Weaponry a tax on the concept since both received close-combat training with weapons and unarmed techniques.<br /> <br /> So where does having a thematic split come up that's important?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008403#post1008403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a tiny difference. Look where your hands are. With weaponry, you're aiming at least a foot away from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as you say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A staff fighter is going to fight differently than a sword fighter... </div> </div> </div>Weaponry covers a wide range of weapon &quot;reach.&quot; A 3-inch knife blade, a foot long machete, and a 12 foot bullwhip are all Weaponry based. Saying that your fists are too &quot;short&quot; to fit into this doesn't really seem to bare out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, it's like the differences here. Science can allow you to appreciate how to build things, but doesn't necessarily let you build things and on its own has a lot more. </div> </div> </div>I think that was meant with the idea that those Skills are examples of Skills that could be broken up similarly to how Brawl and Weaponry are currently, and what combining Brawl and Weaponry would look like in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T01:18:02-08:00","id":1008454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008448#post1008448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the thematic difference important to CofD?<br /> <br /> There are plenty of games were the Brawler and the Swordsman are valuable as thematically different archetypes that they deserve significant representation. Why is it important to break up close-combat fighting into these in the CofD? The vast majority of people that are trained to fight in real world circumstances are trained to fight armed and unarmed. And this has been true for most of history. The thematic appeal to genre doesn't seem to have a lot of place in the CofD. Horror/Urban Fantasy doesn't put much stress on these things (and it can be done when needed with things like Kiths from Changeling where these narrative archetypes matter significantly). The idea that your average street thug needs different Skills for beating you with a baseball bat or kicking your ribs in doesn't seem to bare out. Playing a beat cop or someone that did a tour in Iraq makes having Brawl and Weaponry a tax on the concept since both received close-combat training with weapons and unarmed techniques.<br /> <br /> So where does having a thematic split come up that's important?</div> </div> </div> </div>Posters seem to vary their interests in the game based on the complaint. Sometimes the mechanics don't make sense to someone, sometimes the thematics don't. In this case they both do. But I disagree that it doesn't seem to have a lot of place in Chronicles. Detectives with billy clubs and blackjacks, mooks with 'mitts like iron.' You move past mortal and you have Kung-fu mages and your more standard staff-or-sword wielder. Werewolf especially stands out, as biting is more effective. Even in mortal biting is a Brawl attack, though done with a penalty. Vampires wild and savage ripping opponents apart with their bare hands and fangs, while those who pretend at a certain nobility might wield a blade and fight 'honorably.' <br /> <br /> At what point does it stop being character creation and start being a tax? That point seems a bit of an aside.<br /> <br /> It's the difference between Rocky and Connor MacLeod. Bruce Lee and Conan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Weaponry covers a wide range of weapon &quot;reach.&quot; A 3-inch knife blade, a foot long machete, and a 12 foot bullwhip are all Weaponry based. Saying that your fists are too &quot;short&quot; to fit into this doesn't really seem to bare out. </div> </div> </div>But nothing in Weaponry fits in the 'fist range.' Type while holding a three inch knife blade, or walk on foot-tall stilts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that was meant with the idea that those Skills are examples of Skills that could be broken up similarly to how Brawl and Weaponry are currently, and what combining Brawl and Weaponry would look like in practice. </div> </div> </div>Probably. Anyone's free to do what they want in their games, but based on the kind of stories Chronicles tries to represent it makes sense that Brawl and Weaponry are two separate things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-26-2016, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T02:12:31-08:00","id":1008460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008454#post1008454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I disagree that it doesn't seem to have a lot of place in Chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of your examples explain why a whole separate Skill is needed when equipment choices, Specialties, Merits, and supernatural powers actually exist to cover all of them in terms of specifics. <br /> <br /> How are the thematic value of any of those diminished by merging Brawl and Weaponry? Why is it important for the detective with a billy club to need to invest separately to also have a decent right hook? How is a combat-mage's tool not just a reflection of their Yantra over some need to make punching different from stabbing mechanically more than the weapon bonus for stabbing? How does any of this change the massive difference between a werewolf's bite vs. a human's bite? How is the wild vs. cultured vampire not captured far more in having the Riding the Wave Merit (plus maybe Claws of the Unholy) vs. having the Kindred Dueling Merit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At what point does it stop being character creation and start being a tax? That point seems a bit of an aside. </div> </div> </div>For me? When the two largely become inseparable for the concepts that are going to be the ones most invested in them.<br /> <br /> The point is a reinforcement of the fact that most close-combat training includes unarmed and armed techniques.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's the difference between Rocky and Connor MacLeod. Bruce Lee and Conan. </div> </div> </div>The difference between Rocky and Connor is that Rocky is an athlete who's sport overlaps with part of combat training and Connor is a centuries old warrior that can fight unarmed, and armed with a number of weapons.<br /> <br /> Bruce Lee completely supported learning armed fighting alongside unarmed fighting, and Conan was likewise skilled in both. The difference between them is more of the classic &quot;big strong guy,&quot; vs. &quot;smaller fast guy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But nothing in Weaponry fits in the 'fist range.' Type while holding a three inch knife blade, or walk on foot-tall stilts. </div> </div> </div>The Shiv Merit lets you make a weapon that's small enough to work why either Weaponry or Brawl... so going to say that yes, Weaponry does cover &quot;fist range&quot; esp. as abstract about range as the CofD is.<br /> <br /> Also, try typing while wearing brass knuckles. It doesn't really work well either.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what stilts has to do with any of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone's free to do what they want in their games, but based on the kind of stories Chronicles tries to represent it makes sense that Brawl and Weaponry are two separate things. </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> already pointed out, that despite asserting this, very little in the way of a case for it as ever been made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T11:12:56-08:00","id":1008615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008282#post1008282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can't, but otoh they really don't need to. They have other, very powerful, defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Plasma Drive Demon Form ability lets them, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T23:54:55-08:00","id":1008839,"title":"","content":"Hm I guess it means there would be 5 less dots to put on brawl and weaponry seperately if they were together so could easily be a master of all weapons and fightng no matter your build.<br /> <br /> So on CC you can put dots into other things and max out melee rather than one type.<br /> <br /> It feels kinda unbalanced but brawl isnt really effective for mortals so could work out. Itll be interesting to try it out and see how it effectives the game. The rolls would be the same strength and brawl unless you have fighting finnass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:01:31-08:00","id":1011684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutedMirth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals#post1007970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So most of my players have about 6 defence and one has some decent brawl but found that if I give npcs that type of defence then the brawler of the group is running on a luck die to do anything physical.<br /> <br /> So it kinda feels useless to even put points into strength and brawl at low levels.<br /> <br /> Would it be too game breaking to roll brawl with strength and dex?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, don't assume such level of Defense as default. It means at least <i>very good</i> Dexterity <u>and</u> Wits, and the athletic prowess of a true professional, able to score fairly good at virtually any kind of sport. The ease to produce such numbers in character creation easily makes us forget how uncommon such traits should be. A non-professional ruffian should fall between 2-4 Defense, with the lower spectrum being more common. The Average Joe should be between 1-3, with 2 being by far the most common.<br /> <br /> Second, the 2nd Editions already have this in mind. Equally skilled combatants should be at a Chance Die more often than not by default, even with weapons. Actual dice, so, should represent cleverness, willpower, or other ways to get an edge on the situation. It seems odd, but actually most people will try to find this kind of edge when pressed by actual need of winning the fight, so your players should do this a lot when the combat is dramatically relevant to the story. And when it isn't, you use the fast rules.<br /> <br /> Third, stop thinking about Brawl as a combat option at a game, and try to figure why someone would use it IRL. Not that I don't think that rules need to be well made, but because you're effectively looking for the wrong function. No one with a working brain will think fists are better than actual weapons to &quot;<i>dish damage</i>&quot;. We use brawl primarily for sport, to take on someone without truly wanting to kill, to grapple, or to make for it in situations where a weapon isn't an option. Cops and soldiers are trained in brawl for such situations, not to actually use brawl in place of their other weapons in a combat. When they need to actually hurt, they have at least a batom at hand.<br /> <br /> If you take those three into consideration, you will see brawl getting a niche in your chronicle. It still work against common people fairly well, can be used on situations you can't use a weapon for any reason (heck, you can punch a guy in the face on most situations without breaking any really serious social rule), and have a lot of uses an actual weapon don't have. Just isn't , won't be, and shouldn't be an optimized damage source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:16:23-08:00","id":1012536,"title":"","content":"Yeah, combat is designed so against equally skilled opponent, you want to Willpower+All Out Attack or Willpower+Other Way To Gain Advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:29:53-08:00","id":1042475,"title":"","content":"You're right, it can just as well be combined with some sort of general Combat skill if you want to do that sort of thing. There is differences but it's as much the difference between other Skills and their specialties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:45:01-08:00","id":1042482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1042475#post1042475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, it can just as well be combined with some sort of general Combat skill if you want to do that sort of thing. There is differences but it's as much the difference between other Skills and their specialties.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What'd the replacement be? That seems to be the only reason we don't have a generic &quot;Combat skill&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:50:59-08:00","id":1042483,"title":"","content":"'Combat,' Seems the obvious go-to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:01:03-08:00","id":1042487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1042483#post1042483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Combat,' Seems the obvious go-to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean.... replacement for the Physical skills list, because after merging Brawl and Weaponry into Combat, we'd need to add another skill to make the number of skills in every field equal again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:09:41-08:00","id":1042492,"title":"","content":"You could split the Defense bonus from Athletics into Avoidance and keep Athletics about physical fitness. Or you could use Toughness as some sort of Health and Resilience altering skill. These seem like classic things, though.<br /> <br /> I think there needs to be more stuff to do outside of Combat, though. Support for it, at least, obviously there's a lot you can do. Investigation and the Social system are good steps, as is the Crafting one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-02-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:20:43-08:00","id":1042524,"title":"","content":"I think the big bonus to Brawl is you don't have to carry a weapon. Don't under estimate how useful it can be to walk past a security check point and still be ready for a fight or to be able to tell the police officer that he was armed and you weren't so you put him down hard.<br /> You can always use Brawl if you have normal freedom of movement but carrying a baseball bat or knife is about the limit on the street and in most buildings that's pushing things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:27:02-08:00","id":1042553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1042482#post1042482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What'd the replacement be? That seems to be the only reason we don't have a generic &quot;Combat skill&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I floated something already up thread: Performance to separate out skill with physical arts from verbal arts in Expression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1042524#post1042524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the big bonus to Brawl is you don't have to carry a weapon. Don't under estimate how useful it can be to walk past a security check point and still be ready for a fight or to be able to tell the police officer that he was armed and you weren't so you put him down hard.<br /> You can always use Brawl if you have normal freedom of movement but carrying a baseball bat or knife is about the limit on the street and in most buildings that's pushing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is fairly variable. And there are Brawl weapons (many of which are highly illegal).<br /> <br /> As well, there are entire fighting systems IRL designed around using items that can be easily carried (such as canes) where more obvious weapons would be difficult to keep on you. As well, there's things like the Improvised Weapon Merit that lets you go Jackie Chan on people and attack people with whatever items are around even if they're not traditionally weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T16:22:30-08:00","id":1042660,"title":"","content":"As someone has said before, you have to keep in mind why people in the real world bother to develop and learn barehanded fighting styles. I mean, it's not like we stopped after developing spears and arrows, we still do it to this day. And that's because grappling has always been effective and people have always needed to be able to defend themselves againts it, and also because there was always the chance that you could be disarmed or your weapon might breakdown. And also it's fun to see people punch and wrestle each other. And that's why human characters would have Brawl dots.<br /> <br /> It's a bad idea to make unarmed and armed combat the same skill because that's boring. Violence is an important part of the game. Humans are prey and there are many things that would physically attack them. That's why having characters that are either the best at everything or the worst at everything sucks. It doesn't matter as much if your character is the best at playing all instruments and also giving speeches, because in most games you will never be forced to do either, and the tension will almost never hinge on you not knowing how to play the piano even though you are really good with the guitar. In combat, which is common, an attacker forcing you out of your confort zone is makes the situation interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T16:44:36-08:00","id":1042673,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone's really questioning why Brawl would be something people have. The issue is more of a game issue in how Brawl is significantly less potent for normal human characters in the system.<br /> <br /> As well, where is the line for &quot;boring?&quot; Why isn't it boring for any of the other Skills to not be split up into more Skills?<br /> <br /> Violence is important to the game sure, but there's currently three Skills (Brawl, Firearms, Weaponry) that are almost exclusively focused on violence and an additional Skill (Athletics) that has a major impact on how violence plays out. Cutting out one Skill from violence is not going to make a character be able to rule combat with trivial investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T16:52:26-08:00","id":1042678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1008282#post1008282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can't, but otoh they really don't need to. They have other, very powerful, defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least one Demonic Form ability gives defence against Firearms. Plasma Core or something?<br /> <br /> Prometheans have an Alembic that offers it from memory, though I can't recall which one off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Mummies... I can't remember. Grip of Death allows you to catch bullets in the same manner as catching thrown objects. I don't recall if there's anything that allows you to apply Defence directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T18:03:49-08:00","id":1042720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1042673#post1042673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone's really questioning why Brawl would be something people have. The issue is more of a game issue in how Brawl is significantly less potent for normal human characters in the system.<br /> <br /> As well, where is the line for &quot;boring?&quot; Why isn't it boring for any of the other Skills to not be split up into more Skills?<br /> <br /> Violence is important to the game sure, but there's currently three Skills (Brawl, Firearms, Weaponry) that are almost exclusively focused on violence and an additional Skill (Athletics) that has a major impact on how violence plays out. Cutting out one Skill from violence is not going to make a character be able to rule combat with trivial investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brawl is significant\u00f1y less potent in the system because it is significantly less potent in real life, and as much as the game is fiction and tries doesn't bother too much with realism, it's not a fantasy martial arts game. Not the base game at least.<br /> <br /> By cutting one skill you colapsed two different situations into a single one. The onde with the higher dots has the most chance and there's nothing you can do other than to run away and maybe shoot at them if you have a firearm. Having two skills and having to distribute dots among them creates many more possibilities where a Brawler may get an advantage by grappling, or getting the drop on an opponent when they can't reach a weapon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T19:44:18-08:00","id":1042759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1042720#post1042720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brawl is significant\u00f1y less potent in the system because it is significantly less potent in real life, and as much as the game is fiction and tries doesn't bother too much with realism, it's not a fantasy martial arts game. Not the base game at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>It not being a fantasy martial arts game is all the more reason to not worry about having Brawl and Weaponry. A fantasy martial arts game wants more mechanical detail around fighting so that each character's martial art feels a distinct thematic and mechanical choice.<br /> <br /> Having a trait that costs the same as other traits, but everyone agrees does less for it in the name of &quot;real life&quot; is not a winning argument for a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By cutting one skill you colapsed two different situations into a single one. </div> </div> </div>I haven't changed the potential situations at all. I've simply changed how much investment it takes to be good in multiple situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The onde with the higher dots has the most chance and there's nothing you can do other than to run away and maybe shoot at them if you have a firearm. </div> </div> </div>That's already the case as much as &quot;there's nothing you can do,&quot; only really applies in a white-room sort of situation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having two skills and having to distribute dots among them creates many more possibilities where a Brawler may get an advantage by grappling, or getting the drop on an opponent when they can't reach a weapon. </div> </div> </div>The same thing is accomplished via specialties and Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T08:15:56-08:00","id":1042959,"title":"","content":"You have melee 3 with sword specialty. You are grappled. You still have melee 3. You have weaponry 3 with a sword specialty. You are grappled. You are at -1 penalty. You really don't see that's a much more dramatic difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:47:44-08:00","id":1043069,"title":"","content":"I understand the math just fine.<br /> <br /> The problem that you're fundamentally not addressing, is why that difference matters to the kind of drama that game aims for.<br /> <br /> I do not care, in the slightest, if in my CofD games the differences between a &quot;grappler&quot; and a &quot;swordsman&quot; is 1-2 dice, equipment selection, and Merit selection. That's enough for me, because:<br /> <br /> 1) The kinds of characters that in the RAW would justify high Brawl + low/no Weaponry or low/no Brawl + high Weaponry are not characters I find compelling or interesting to the setting. Every major school of practical close combat fighting teaches both Brawl and Weaponry. An Olympic fencer is not inherently a skilled combatant. I would rather see that modeled with high Athletics + low Melee + Fencing as Specialty boosted with Interdisciplinary Specialty and Area of Expertise. So our fencer can dominate in sport fighting, be a threat in real fighting if in their comfort zone, and screwed in real fighting if removed from it.<br /> <br /> 2) We have a giant number of combat Merits in the game. Even with identical Attributes and Skills, Merit selection matters a ton to a character's best mode of up-close violence. Give these two otherwise identical characters 5 dots in Merits related to a specific strategy (grappling, light weapons, etc.) and those Merits will easily ensure one character has the advantage in their chosen best mode.<br /> <br /> 3) Incentivizing characters towards high/low distributions of Brawl and Weaponry does not create the kinds of dramatic scenes of violence I feel the CofD attempts to model. I don't want players mono-focusing on punches and kicks because picking up a trash can and hitting the other guy with it in a back alley beat down would mean having to use Weaponry and thus costs them too many dice. If a character wakes up to hear a Slasher breaking into their home, I don't want them to grab a knife and just use that because they're Weaponry focused. I want them to try ideas like waiting at the top of the stairs and trying to kill the assailant to knock them down those stairs.<br /> <br /> Basically, I want violence in the CofD to allow for characters that invest in violence to solve problems the ability to specialize in a form of it, but I want the game to flow creatively without the players having to weigh the pros and cons of different ideas. I want the players to use the scene to make scenes of violence that have the grit the CofD aims for by trying to find whatever advantage they can muster to sway the tide of a fight rather than violence getting monotonous because they always stick to the same thing as their best/only thing and then get annoyed because challenging them turns binary (&quot;I have my sword, I carve up opponents with ease&quot; or &quot;I am unarmed, I'm boned, I don't like the ST for taking my sword away&quot;).<br /> <br /> Nothing you're saying, or anyone said before, has put a dent in convincing me that Brawl + Weaponry is better towards these goals than a unified close-combat Skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T20:56:08-08:00","id":1043352,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I also feel that Violence should be an umbrella skill like Academics or Science. A lot to be gained, and while some things are also lost, I feel they are worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T02:35:30-08:00","id":1043437,"title":"","content":"The problem I have with combining them into a single skill is that it makes combat characters much, much more versatile, and more versatility equals more power (because the number of situations in which you can utilize your power grows with versatility, granting you power in situations you would not have had it otherwise).<br /> <br /> I can understand why it would work for some games, but in mine I really don't want combat characters getting that power increase from versatility without making sacrifices in other areas like they currently have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:54:24-08:00","id":1043581,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that if your high weapon skill character is boned for losing their sword because they lacked in training their brawl. Narratively that's more interesting than oh no matter my character knows that coz melee skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:01:13-08:00","id":1043665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043437#post1043437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I have with combining them into a single skill is that it makes combat characters much, much more versatile, and more versatility equals more power (because the number of situations in which you can utilize your power grows with versatility, granting you power in situations you would not have had it otherwise).</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that just saying, &quot;much&quot; a lot doesn't equate to demonstrating this to be the case.<br /> <br /> What's the versatility achieved?<br /> <br /> Some Merits now have effectively lower prerequisites sure, but close combat is still the most Merit intensive part of the game. Access to more Fighting Merits is greater versatility, but each of those Merits still costs you investment elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Unarmed focused characters have a greater versatility of equipment. This is ultimately part of the whole point. Brawl's biggest issue is its lack of equipment options that allow it to be competitive with Weaponry, forcing Brawl characters to rely on Merits and/or supernatural powers to have the weight in combat a Weaponry character has naturally. This increase in power is meant to close this gap.<br /> <br /> Armed focused characters have access to grappling/non-lethal disabling without special equipment (since that exists) and unarmed attacks. How potent is this really? The increased versatility with attacks that deal lower and worse quality damage, and likely lower dice-pools... isn't really even much of an increase outside of a white-room where there's almost always something you can pickup and attack people with.<br /> <br /> So, where does this increase in versatility really equate to such a significant overall change in power for a combat focused character?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutedMirth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043581#post1043581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that if your high weapon skill character is boned for losing their sword because they lacked in training their brawl. Narratively that's more interesting than oh no matter my character knows that coz melee skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is... were does this high Weaponry character with no Brawl training come from?<br /> <br /> I've pointed this out many time already. It may be a fun/interesting situation, but it makes no sense for it to ever actually happen in the nature of the game. How does someone get to 3+ in Weaponry without at least a few dots in Brawl?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T12:48:44-08:00","id":1043687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043069#post1043069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem that you're fundamentally not addressing, is why that difference matters to the kind of drama that game aims for.<br /> <br /> I do not care, in the slightest, if in my CofD games the differences between a &quot;grappler&quot; and a &quot;swordsman&quot; is 1-2 dice, equipment selection, and Merit selection. That's enough for me, because:<br /> <br /> 1) The kinds of characters that in the RAW would justify high Brawl + low/no Weaponry or low/no Brawl + high Weaponry are not characters <b>I find compelling or interesting to the setting</b>. Every major school of practical close combat fighting teaches both Brawl and Weaponry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other people might disagree and consider especially those compelling and/or interesting. What if I want to portray a character who learned down'n'dirty fighting on the streets, but never had a knife in his hands? Don't tell me a world class boxer could properly use a knife in a fight, his athletism and combat experience might help him, but he would make the same mistakes as everyone else who would have to fight with a knife for the first time. What about the school ringer going to olympia: why should he be able to properly use any sort of weapon?<br /> I also like the Kendoka/HEMA-guy who is good with a sword or similar stuff, but since he never paid attention to unarmed fighting is not really good at that.<br /> Because those are fairly realistic guys. Not every character is primary physical skills. Even in the case of the police/soldiers, they'd have farily little brawl and weaponry. If it's not their thing, and they don't train it as a hobby, either, I'd say up to 2 dots, at the most. Because those are supplementary skills, not their bread and butter.<br /> A &quot;martial artist&quot; that is dedicated, like a Shaolin Monk or Maasaki Hatsumi's high-ranking live-in students, now that is someone I would buy having brawl 3+ and weaponry 3+.<br /> <br /> Also, I disagree with &quot;every major school of practical close combat fighting teaches both Brawl and Weaponry&quot;: they get a peek, yes, but the majority does not spend enough time on weaponry that it would warrant more than 1 dot of weaponry, if even that. Most of the schools teach a few forms with an (usually outdated) weapon.<br /> Some really focus on it, e.g. some Silat styles come to mind, some Filipino stuff, one Krav Maga school I visited in Berlin, but those are certainly not the majority.<br /> Not even taking into account that Martial Arts is one of the areas with the most bullshit going around.<br /> <br /> As is always said in the book: change the rules to fit your troupe! I know I wouldn't want a general melee skill, because I LOVE the seperation of &quot;low-lethality threat&quot; fighters and &quot;high-lethality threat&quot; fighters. For most of the reasons already mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T14:01:11-08:00","id":1043720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043665#post1043665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The problem is... were does this high Weaponry character with no Brawl training come from?<br /> <br /> I've pointed this out many time already. It may be a fun/interesting situation, but it makes no sense for it to ever actually happen in the nature of the game. How does someone get to 3+ in Weaponry without at least a few dots in Brawl?</div> </div> </div> </div>You see it as a problem, I see it as a character concept challenge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alisha Goodhardt is nearing the finals in baseball, she's been working hard to pitch and bat to make it to the big leagues, but she still has to have a second job to pay the bills. The owner of the local gas station is pleased the robberies have dropped since she started working there. Alisha really does have a mean swing for a girl which is why they always underestimate her and regret it. She's got quite the fan base now. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rufus Shingles has the shady look of a weasel. He's really nothing special to look at and a strong gust of wind could knock him over. His switchblade though. Always playing with it. It's memorising. Until you realise you're bleeding. They say to never turn your back on Rufus Shingles, but even your front isn't safe from his blade. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hiran <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Patel</span></span> is a weeb. He's fascinated with samurai culture and has taken up Iaido evening classes after college. He'd be competing if it wasn't for his anxieties and although he hates being touched or touching people, he has honed his skill using his sword handle to fight in close combat. It's less elegant in real life situations but it helped him to escape in a mugging attempt without needlessly touching them once. </div> </div> </div>Three characters off the top of my head. Some people focus on one thing they like or are good with. Some never get professional training to do both and learn it on the fly.<br /> <br /> The opposite is also true. Most night classes or universities classes either don't teach you to use a weapon or go against one or they will but it'll cost extra. I did mixed martial arts for several years and learnt self defence, but I couldn't use a weapon efficiently if at all because I had little training in it and I didn't feel the need to pursue it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T14:40:36-08:00","id":1043738,"title":"","content":"Personally, I have to ask this - Where do socialite PCs with 5 Persuasion and no dots in Socialize or Expression come in? How about the occultist with no dots in academics or the fundamentals of science like many do? <br /> <br /> *shrugs* Ideally, you should have PCs that cover all these. Yes, I agree that most people trained in some kind of fighting should have weaponry and brawl. And, in the case of police, the military and often criminals, should have firearms as well. But just as you don't force socialites or intelectuals to have all the skills that normally one would have for their concept, I see no reason to force physical characters eithers. That's just somethign we have to accept as part of the game, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T17:11:54-08:00","id":1043776,"title":"","content":"Yes, a coherent weaponry 5 guy would have a decent brawl. But it would be an aditional expenditure. You'll never see a Weaponry 5 Brawl 5 Firearms 5 character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T21:06:13-08:00","id":1043844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043687#post1043687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other people might disagree and consider especially those compelling and/or interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other people are certainly disagreeing. I just don't see them making a fairly compelling case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if I want to portray a character who learned down'n'dirty fighting on the streets, but never had a knife in his hands? </div> </div> </div>How has he never held a knife, or a club, or a metal pipe, or a glass bottle, or a shiv, or etc. and still be a &quot;down'n'dirty&quot; street fighter? He's never picked up a trash can or a wooden board to smash an opponent with?<br /> <br /> And you still have Merits and Specialties to be more monofocused if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't tell me a world class boxer could properly use a knife in a fight, his athletism and combat experience might help him, but he would make the same mistakes as everyone else who would have to fight with a knife for the first time. What about the school ringer going to olympia: why should he be able to properly use any sort of weapon? </div> </div> </div>A world class boxer is an athlete, not a fighter. They don't have the training to use kicks and grapples, but the current rules say that if your sport boxer takes a lot of Brawl, he's good at those without practical experience.<br /> <br /> Taking Weaponry 4 and saying your character has only used a rapier doesn't mean mechanically they're not capable of using a spear with zero experience or training with one.<br /> <br /> Accepting the broadness of the Skills is already part of the game.<br /> <br /> And as I said already, I would model anything that's &quot;sport&quot; focused as Athletics focused with Interdisciplinary Specialty a low dots in &quot;Melee&quot; to represent their lack of practical combat skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I disagree with &quot;every major school of practical close combat fighting teaches both Brawl and Weaponry&quot;: they get a peek, yes, but the majority does not spend enough time on weaponry that it would warrant more than 1 dot of weaponry, if even that. Most of the schools teach a few forms with an (usually outdated) weapon.<br /> Some really focus on it, e.g. some Silat styles come to mind, some Filipino stuff, one Krav Maga school I visited in Berlin, but those are certainly not the majority.<br /> Not even taking into account that Martial Arts is one of the areas with the most bullshit going around. </div> </div> </div>Most of what you're talking about seems to be places that wouldn't justify more than Brawl 1-2 anyway (you know, basic self defense focused places, not places training people expecting to fight as part of a job or for survival).<br /> <br /> Also original Krav Maga absolutely includes weapon training, even if there are watered down versions of it out there. Krava Maga is based on military combat training, which includes using knifes, rifle stocks, trenching tools,and clubs when necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know I wouldn't want a general melee skill, because I LOVE the seperation of &quot;low-lethality threat&quot; fighters and &quot;high-lethality threat&quot; fighters. For most of the reasons already mentioned. </div> </div> </div>Nothing stops you from having a low lethality fighter in a combined trait. Just focus on Specialties and Merits that focused on unarmed fighting and supportive equipment. You're still going to be doing Bashing attacks and grappling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutedMirth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043720#post1043720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three characters off the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>You notice how all three of these examples are characters that aren't just &quot;Weaponry&quot; focused. They're specific weapon focused. All of them make no sense with high Weaponry. They make sense as low Weaponry with Merits/Specialties to represent their dedication to a single weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most night classes or universities classes either don't teach you to use a weapon or go against one or they will but it'll cost extra. </div> </div> </div>I've never seen that. <b>Every</b> one of these I've every seen that is not a sport (like Kendo) has taught weapon use, and defense against weapons. University self defense classes esp. teach how do use readily available nominally improvised weapons to make up for most of the students not having the raw power or training to really smack someone without the added force of a weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043738#post1043738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I have to ask this - Where do socialite PCs with 5 Persuasion and no dots in Socialize or Expression come in? How about the occultist with no dots in academics or the fundamentals of science like many do?</div> </div> </div> </div>The socialite example is a bit odd, since that would be Socialize is what a socialite would default towards. Expression, Persuasion, and Socialize are all fairly distinct in ways that don't have the same sort of overlap as Brawl and Weaponry.<br /> <br /> While many characters would want levels in each to be an effective social character, a con-artist doesn't need to be good at giving speeches and writing poems, or be able to fit in at a $5K plate fundraiser. They just need to set their targets to scams that don't rely on those things. A party planner doesn't give speeches or paint portraits of the guests, and they aren't there to sway people to specific ways of thinking. Etc.<br /> <br /> The issue here is that each of those as a distinct narrative purpose. Brawl and Weaponry have the same purpose: beating people in close combat violence. The only thing the separates them are the mechanical options available to them to achieve that goal. You can't Socialize really hard and have a poem fall out. You can't Expression really hard and plan a wedding. You can't Persuade really hate and turn your fast-talking into a painting.<br /> <br /> Hitting people with Weaponry and hitting people with Brawl have the same overall results.<br /> <br /> Occult is an odd Skill in general, because (somewhat like Medicine compared to Science) it's a highly specialized version of Academics with a bit of Investigation. I do think Occult should work more like Esoterica in M20, where it's more like Medicine in that it's about application, not knowledge. This does play out in everything that's not a pure-normal human to a large extent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043776#post1043776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a coherent weaponry 5 guy would have a decent brawl. But it would be an aditional expenditure. You'll never see a Weaponry 5 Brawl 5 Firearms 5 character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T02:34:44-08:00","id":1043898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043844#post1043844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Other people are certainly disagreeing. I just don't see them making a fairly compelling case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part I had highlighted was to point out that this is what you like, e.g. your taste. And taste differs. I wouldn't mind a more <i>diverse </i>brawl/weaponry system, but it's fine the way it is imo. As for compelling case, I am not convinced by your arguments; does that mean you do not make a compelling case?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043844#post1043844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How has he never held a knife, or a club, or a metal pipe, or a glass bottle, or a shiv, or etc. and still be a &quot;down'n'dirty&quot; street fighter? He's never picked up a trash can or a wooden board to smash an opponent with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Io and behold, yes those types of people still exist. I personally know two who used to live like that, but they drew a strong line, which is probably what helped them get out in the first place. In game terms, this is something where Aspirations and/or Virtue and Vice would come in, I believe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043844#post1043844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A world class boxer is an athlete, not a fighter. They don't have the training to use kicks and grapples, but the current rules say that if your sport boxer takes a lot of Brawl, he's good at those without practical experience.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nowhere does it say he's good with kicks, since those are fluff, anyway. The way I see it, he is good in combat situations and can tell when someone feints or is going to attack (if you telegraph, you telegraph, doesn't matter HOW you want to attack), so he can make some distance or make use of it.<br /> A good roll against him could be a lowkick, a poor roll against him is someone trying to box with a boxer, his poor roll could be him attempting to kick and do poorly, a good roll him getting a good hook in etc. That way, fluff and system conform.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043844#post1043844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of what you're talking about seems to be places that wouldn't justify more than Brawl 1-2 anyway (you know, basic self defense focused places, not places training people expecting to fight as part of a job or for survival).<br /> <br /> Also original Krav Maga absolutely includes weapon training, even if there are watered down versions of it out there. Krava Maga is based on military combat training, which includes using knifes, rifle stocks, trenching tools,and clubs when necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Krav Maga school as well as Silat Suffian Bela Diri etc. were mentioned as GOOD examples, giving weapons not just some attention on the side, but going 50/50 or close to it.<br /> Sorry if that wasn't clear from the way I wrote.<br /> <br /> IMO, most people wouldn't be able to have more than Brawl 2 anyway. 4-5 are for professionals, 3 being the overlap of those doing it for fun and being really good at it, so maybe considering going pro. 1-3 is what the majority of schools would provide for. Hence my disagreement with &quot;majority of martial arts schools teach both&quot;.<br /> Btw, since boxers are athletes, what about MMA fighters? Those guys often have 0 weaponry, but brawl 5 is totally what I would use to translate e.g. Jon Jones into CofD.<br /> And what about HEMA/Iaido/Kendo ? Those guys often know very little to nothing about straight hand-to-hand combat. Canne de combat? Kyudo and Gungsol? Itto-Ryu? Donga?<br /> I simply disagree that someone with weaponry 3+ NEEDS to have more than one dot in brawl (if even that, because I consider fencing a legit martial sport and thus a valid base for weaponry), based on my personal experiences.<br /> Similarly, I also feel a system that keeps one melee stat and works mostly through merits is less transparent, and still am not convinced that it wouldn't be cheaper, xp-wise.<br /> High Brawl AND high Weaponry are the hallmark of a primary physically skilled martial artist, and the amount of xp put in is reflected through their ability to dish out the hurt under all circumstances. My personal opinion is, this reflects the necessary training and focus well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-05-2017, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T05:17:45-08:00","id":1043927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043844#post1043844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The socialite example is a bit odd, since that would be Socialize is what a socialite would default towards. Expression, Persuasion, and Socialize are all fairly distinct in ways that don't have the same sort of overlap as Brawl and Weaponry.</div> </div> </div> </div> Clearly you haven't seen the same PCs I have. Socialite style PCs pick and choose skills to min-max their abilities all the time. And, yes, they all do have overlap. <br /> <br /> That's my whole point. Brawl and Weaponry are not the only skills out there with overlap. You're correct in that overlap exists, but you are mistaken if you think that's the only situation where such overlap exists. It might not be as clear, given that combat is such a predominant subsystem in this game that's seen lots of use while Social Maneuvering, Chases, Building Equipment and Investigation gets much less spotlight time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A party planner doesn't give speeches or paint portraits of the guests, and they aren't there to sway people to specific ways of thinking. Etc. </div> </div> </div> If you think a party planner isn't there to sway people's minds to specific ways of thinking, then I'm sorry, you have no idea what goes into professional party planning. Party planning is an art form on its own that does require applications of Expression (decorations), arranging entertainment (socialize), reading crowds in real time and altering plans as necessary (empathy), picking seating (politics), and more. And that doesn't touch on the fact that parties have an end goal in mind to achieve- sometimes that's to just have fun, but other times its to convince people to donate to a cause, or to gather allies, or to make plans. <br /> <br /> Your other examples aren't much better either. You're ignoring the complexity involved in these things for the sake of your argument, which is undermining your position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue here is that each of those as a distinct narrative purpose. Brawl and Weaponry have the same purpose: beating people in close combat violence. The only thing the separates them are the mechanical options available to them to achieve that goal. You can't Socialize really hard and have a poem fall out. You can't Expression really hard and plan a wedding. You can't Persuade really hate and turn your fast-talking into a painting.<br /> <br /> Hitting people with Weaponry and hitting people with Brawl have the same overall results. </div> </div> </div> Except that you're ignoring the similarities and blowing up the differences. Sure, brawl and weaponry both deal damage in close combat. But Persuasion, Expression, Empathy and Socialize can all be used to Open Doors to seduce someone. Investigate, Science, Medicine, etc can all be used to gather Clues as evideince to track down a killer. Firearms, Athletics, Brawl and Weaponry, the four main &quot;combat skills,&quot; share in common the fact that they're all used as a major part of the combat subsystem in order to deal damage. That's kind of what the Combat subsystem does. But anytime you use any subsystem, no matter what skill you choose, its going to have a similar result. Dealing damage, opening doors, finding clues, outracing someone, etc. <br /> <br /> Brawl skill encompasses different things outside of dealing damage. Weaponry includes not only how to use weapons, but how to inspect and upkeep them. In this case, you actually have more in common with the Firearm skill, which includes inspection and upkeep of guns, than with Brawl - the only real narrative distinction is that one is used at ranged. The only thing Athletics has in common with the others is that it can deal damage with thrown items and adds into Defense. So, so much you can do with Athletics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And, you know what? Lets put this another way. Lets say that we make all your Melee Damage as a skill. Melee Damaging is NOT a good skill for grappling; in your words, they have distinct narrative purposes. The techniques you use for hurting someone with a grapple, the muscles you use, the actions you take are all distinct. There's no good way of combining them. So, now we STILL have two distinct skills for melee action - damage and grappling. The only acomplishment is that you moved dealing damage with a fist and feet to another skill. And THEN we're going to have people who bring up arguments about boxers and other close combat specialists who never train with weapons but use fists, feet and grappling interchangably. So, we haven't even silenced any debate on the matter either. The net result is just tweaking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you don't find any of this to be compelling arguments, then perhaps this is just a question of your personal tastes. You want it that way, so go ahead and rule it that way. Like I said, its not going to change much in the long run. This isn't a primary combat game, and even when it is combat, its more violence to break people's will to resist than it is epic fights with delicate tweaking of balance. Mind control, animal/retainer/shapeshifted swarms, guns, sneak attacks, spells, and automobile crashes are all combat factors that happen. Its such a tiny detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T05:19:11-08:00","id":1043928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043776#post1043776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a coherent weaponry 5 guy would have a decent brawl. But it would be an aditional expenditure. You'll never see a Weaponry 5 Brawl 5 Firearms 5 character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Challenge accepted<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T05:23:26-08:00","id":1043929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043928#post1043928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Challenge accepted</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you can accomplish it if you set out specifically to do it. It's only 30 xp tops buying from zero. But that would be as artificial as a Weaponry 5 Brawl 0 guy people were saying would never actually exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T05:46:55-08:00","id":1043935,"title":"","content":"Also I just want to point out that clinching IS part of boxing, even if there very specific rules about it. To the point where many boxing fans rail against it as a lame tactic. A Boxer with no cross training would be lost against a true grappler (someone with specialties and a Style), but against a regular joe or simple thug trying to tackle or hold him down he wouldn't be out of his comfort zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T05:50:13-08:00","id":1043938,"title":"","content":"Awww... take all the fun out of it, why don't you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T06:48:54-08:00","id":1043959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043069#post1043069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3) Incentivizing characters towards high/low distributions of Brawl and Weaponry does not create the kinds of dramatic scenes of violence I feel the CofD attempts to model. I don't want players mono-focusing on punches and kicks because picking up a trash can and hitting the other guy with it in a back alley beat down would mean having to use Weaponry and thus costs them too many dice. If a character wakes up to hear a Slasher breaking into their home, I don't want them to grab a knife and just use that because they're Weaponry focused. I want them to try ideas like waiting at the top of the stairs and trying to kill the assailant to knock them down those stairs.</div> </div> </div> </div> I find these examples to be particularly amusing during this argument. Wanting characters to pick up trash cans and hitting guys with it has nothign to do with merging Brawl and Weaponry. Or, rather, ti has everything to do with it, because its an expression of using the Shiv merit with Improvised Weaponry - combining the different Street Style fighting merits. In short - you're asking to not only fold Brawl and Weaponry to allow your example, but also folding Fighting Merits into the skills. This puts a lie to your &quot;specialization if they want&quot; because your'e attempting to push specialzing onto the generic skills.<br /> <br /> Why would people pick up a knife if they're tracking down a Slasher? <i>Because knives are better defensive weapons than trying to knock someone bigger and stronger than you down stairs</i>. Why, in the name of all that is holy, would anyone think that not having a weapon when a murderer is around you is a good thing? That's kind of silly. Knives are always going to be better than not. Plus, you're attempting a Knock Down Tilt if you're talking about dropping them down stairs. Grabbing a knife is always going to make that attempt easier - or, at least, its always going do more damage during the attack. The argument here is pretty bad because, irregardless if we're talking about a Melee skill or Weaponry skill, you're grabbing that knife. People are goign to be thinking about numbers, irregardless if we're talking about merged skills or not. 0B is not equivalent to 1L. Realistically, though, no matter the skill dots, our ambusher should be actually grabbing something Size 2 and avoid any penalty to the roll to Knock Down in the first place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:20:32-08:00","id":1044214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043898#post1043898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for compelling case, I am not convinced by your arguments; does that mean you do not make a compelling case?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to feel that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I personally know two who used to live like that, but they drew a strong line, which is probably what helped them get out in the first place. In game terms, this is something where Aspirations and/or Virtue and Vice would come in, I believe? </div> </div> </div>Actually I would argue this is exactly why a unified close combat Skill is better for the kind of game we're talking about.<br /> <br /> &quot;Drawing a strong line.&quot; on a moral issue is meaningless if the game makes this choice mechanically superior. In the RAW, this choice has no really narrative power to it, because they take Brawl and related Merits, and ignore Weaponry. There's no <b>temptation</b> to pick up a weapon, because mechanically it's stupid for them to. In the game, instead of, &quot;I choose to take the harder path on moral grounds,&quot; it's, &quot;I'm going Brawl, so my best choice is to go 100% Brawl, so the choice to not use weapons is always mechanically superior for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> With a unified &quot;Melee,&quot; these guys are making a real choice in the system. With Brawl and Weaponry, it's not a moral choice, it's just a descriptive choice.<br /> <br /> If a character should roll Integrity as a Breaking Point for using a weapon instead of their fists (since that's probably more where this would come up over Aspirations/Anchors), and dumps all their combat stuff into Brawl and then never has a reason to face that Breaking point. If they take &quot;Melee&quot; every weapon around them is temptation to risk that Breaking Point. Every time combat is starting to go against them, they're making a meaningful choice to stick to their convictions, or compromise to win.<br /> <br /> That's what I want out of CofD games. Meaningful character decisions. Not just fluffed up reasons to have Brawl 5/Weaponry 0.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nowhere does it say he's good with kicks, since those are fluff, anyway. </div> </div> </div>And he suffers what penalty to kick someone instead of punching?<br /> <br /> The &quot;it's just fluff' thing works just as well for my points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way I see it, he is good in combat situations and can tell when someone feints or is going to attack (if you telegraph, you telegraph, doesn't matter HOW you want to attack), so he can make some distance or make use of it. </div> </div> </div>So... he's got good Attributes and high Athletics for a naturally high Defense/Dodge. Even when out of his element as a sportsman, he can put his Skills to good use to see attacks coming and get out of the way.<br /> <br /> That doesn't address how good he is in combat situations without refs, without rounds and breaks, and with having to overcome all the training that says, &quot;you can't do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of the Mythbusters: the Search episode from this weekend, where they tested &quot;reverse&quot; bikes that have a gearing system that reverse the steering column on the bike so that what normally turns you right turns you left instead. And all the contestants failed horribly just trying to go 12 feet. It takes significant practice, like learning to ride all over again, to get the hang of it. Participants in &quot;combat&quot; sports in real fights face the same sort of situation. All the rules and training for the sport gets in the way when fighting someone that's used to not having rules. Their training is a hindrance until they actually get experience outside of the ring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hence my disagreement with &quot;majority of martial arts schools teach both&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Which is why I didn't say that. I said the majority of practical combat schools teach both. People being trained to fight in the real world, not people being trained to master an archaic weapon, or participate in sports, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Btw, since boxers are athletes, what about MMA fighters? </div> </div> </div>MMA at first was a bit more of this, but has grown increasingly closer to other combat sports as it has grown in popularity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what about HEMA </div> </div> </div>Just singling this out, HEMA people that ignore grappling and strikes... aren't really doing HEMA justice. All the combat manuals show that these styles were meant to include Brawl in their application. People studying HEMA for show? OK, but why are they any good in a real fight? People that do serious HEMA all agree that it should include &quot;unarmed&quot; and grapple maneuvers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I simply disagree that someone with weaponry 3+ NEEDS to have more than one dot in brawl (if even that, because I consider fencing a legit martial sport and thus a valid base for weaponry), based on my personal experiences. </div> </div> </div>And given the high focus of every example listed, I've yet to here a single reason why Melee 1 + Specialty + Merits doesn't handle these highly focused styles being dangerous when allowed to operate in their comfort zone, but in danger when taken out of it. If anything, that's a better model than Weaponry 3/Brawl 1, because most of them aren't trained in any weapon, but very specific weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, I also feel a system that keeps one melee stat and works mostly through merits is less transparent, and still am not convinced that it wouldn't be cheaper, xp-wise. </div> </div> </div>What does &quot;less transparent&quot; even mean in this?<br /> <br /> And I never said it wouldn't be cheaper XP-wise, just that there's still a significant investment in being really good at specific tactics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> High Brawl AND high Weaponry are the hallmark of a primary physically skilled martial artist, and the amount of xp put in is reflected through their ability to dish out the hurt under all circumstances. My personal opinion is, this reflects the necessary training and focus well. </div> </div> </div>This is essentially a circular argument that comes down to, &quot;The system models it this way, so that's how it should be modeled.&quot;<br /> <br /> The system doesn't care about &quot;realistic&quot; XP investment. Science 5 is insanely broad competency for half the cost...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043927#post1043927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly you haven't seen the same PCs I have. Socialite style PCs pick and choose skills to min-max their abilities all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how min-maxing has anything to do with what was being said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, yes, they all do have overlap. </div> </div> </div>Never claimed otherwise. My claim is the significance of the amount of overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're correct in that overlap exists, but you are mistaken if you think that's the only situation where such overlap exists. </div> </div> </div>So, I'm right, and I'm not mistaken. Glad to see that recognized...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you think a party planner isn't there to sway people's minds to specific ways of thinking, then I'm sorry, you have no idea what goes into professional party planning. </div> </div> </div>I think I have a few friends that would be pretty insulted by the idea that their profession is apparently factually 100% about manipulating people.<br /> <br /> I know a few event planners. One of them focuses on fundraising, and yeah, they're exactly what you're talking about. One of them is a wedding planner... and is not there to make statements, they're there to make the wedding happen.<br /> <br /> Two of them focus on entertainment events (one does a lot of parties, the other does more conventions and stuff like that). One of them just wants to create spaces for people to have a good time. The other wants to use them to promote certain things; but he kinda sucks at it.<br /> <br /> The last two are also the best examples of why this things are distinct. The first (while he has high Empathy anyway) is a very hands off organizer. He has a people. He has clients. He gets them together. He trusts his employees and regular third party service providers to do their work. Decorations, food, music? He doesn't do any of that. He has people that handle that.<br /> <br /> The second is a micromanager. He wants to be involved in everything, but isn't nearly as good at the people he hires, and constantly frustrates his staff because of it. He has all these Skills, but not well enough to actually do what he's trying.<br /> <br /> I also see the little goal post shift there of adding in another two Skills in there.<br /> <br /> Though I do not see the justification of requiring Politics to handle seating arrangements at a party. Socialize as written seems to have that completely covered. Empathy is more of a gray area, but even there Socialize as written implies you can tell how a party is going with Socialize without having to have Empathy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that doesn't touch on the fact that parties have an end goal in mind to achieve- sometimes that's to just have fun, but other times its to convince people to donate to a cause, or to gather allies, or to make plans. </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you're a political event specialist, you're going to want a broader ability set than someone that plans weddings. I didn't say there's no reason to not have investment in multiple Skills for party planning, but that the general &quot;party planner&quot; Skill is Socialize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that you're ignoring the similarities and blowing up the differences. </div> </div> </div>No. You're blowing up the similarities and ignoring the differences.<br /> <br /> And since you seem to think that counts as making a meaningful point, I think you should just acknowledge that as the case and we can move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Persuasion, Expression, Empathy and Socialize can all be used to Open Doors to seduce someone. </div> </div> </div>No. Any Skill (even Brawl!) can be used to Open Doors. Seducing someone is Persuasion. If you're trying to Open Doors with seduction, it's a Persuasion roll. As well, the Opening all of someone's doors doesn't make them seduced. The system compels an action. You can Open Doors on someone into going out with a date with you, and then use Persuasion to seduce them. You can't Open Doors until they're seduced. If you want to seduce someone, it's Persuasion. Even if you use Social Maneuvering and other Skills to create situations to allow more Persuasion attempts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Firearms, Athletics, Brawl and Weaponry, the four main &quot;combat skills,&quot; share in common the fact that they're all used as a major part of the combat subsystem in order to deal damage. </div> </div> </div>Well, the bigger issue really is that Brawl, Firearms, and Weaponry have extremely little application outside of combat systems and Hard Leverage. Athletics has lots of other uses.<br /> <br /> If there were more subsystems that made greater and more distinctive use of the differences between the three &quot;attack&quot; Skills, the whole subsystem argument would be a lot more meaningful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Melee Damaging is NOT a good skill for grappling; </div> </div> </div>This is a bit of a strawman.<br /> <br /> It is not &quot;Melee Damaging.&quot; Just &quot;Melee.&quot; as in close combat fighting skills. Which is just fine for grappling. Firing a bow, a rifle, and a mortar all use the same Skill, the &quot;muscle&quot; thing has no bearing on this.<br /> <br /> Nothing in this reflects what I'm actually advocating for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1043959#post1043959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find these examples to be particularly amusing during this argument. Wanting characters to pick up trash cans and hitting guys with it has nothign to do with merging Brawl and Weaponry.</div> </div> </div> </div>This literally makes no sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, rather, ti has everything to do with it, because its an expression of using the Shiv merit with Improvised Weaponry - combining the different Street Style fighting merits. </div> </div> </div>The Shiv merit uses prepared weapons, and isn't valid with Improvised Weaponry.<br /> <br /> Improvised Weaponry doesn't change, since it's basically an expanded version of Quick Draw at the first dot without having to specialize like Quick Draw, and the later dots keep doing what they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short - you're asking to not only fold Brawl and Weaponry to allow your example, but also folding Fighting Merits into the skills. </div> </div> </div>Nothing in my suggestion says that the normal rules for readying weapons, or the Merits that interact with that, change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This puts a lie to your &quot;specialization if they want&quot; because your'e attempting to push specialzing onto the generic skills. </div> </div> </div>It puts a lie to a strawman argument. You seem extremely dead set on making my suggestion something that I'm not saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would people pick up a knife if they're tracking down a Slasher? </div> </div> </div>The CofD is a designed to encourage tropes that aren't not always optimal tactics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:41:52-08:00","id":1044229,"title":"","content":"This is where I feel that Specialties are criminally underused in CofD. I would love unified Violence skill, where Violence 5 is master of all forms of inflicting ouchies (by the way, according to CoD Core, 2 dots in something is already professional level! don't underestimate how important these early dots are) and Violence 1 (Punching, Boxing, Sport Fights, Right Hook, All Out) person is box master who isn't that good about stabbing you with pointy bits. <br /> Note that the Boxer is less XP intensive (Master Assassin spent 10 XP on becoming master of all ouchies, Boxer spent 7, and is actually better at boxing than Ouchie Master with smaller basic Violence), so there is a real incentive to go &quot;Master Swordsman&quot; or even &quot;Night Class Iaido Student&quot;. Hell, I wish it was an official rule that you can take a Specialty in a skill with 0 dots for this explicit reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T22:56:05-08:00","id":1044395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1044229#post1044229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hell, I wish it was an official rule that you can take a Specialty in a skill with 0 dots for this explicit reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's a fun house rule to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T03:51:16-08:00","id":1044432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1044214#post1044214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It puts a lie to a strawman argument. You seem extremely dead set on making my suggestion something that I'm not saying.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, I'm saying that your suggestions are unrealistic; you're saying things will magically happen if you but merge Brawl and Weaponry, but only so long as ignore a ton of other factors that have an impact. As well, you're attributing motivations to players (ie caring about dots and numbers) that will magically disappear with a merger while ignoring that such players who care about numbers will be considering other numbers. Players will care about having to waste their combat actions to pick up random trash, about having -1 damage from poor weapons, about initiative penalties and more. You are also twisting how other systems work to favor your interpretation above all others, all the while applying a double standard to skills outside of combat ones.<br /> <br /> The benefits you claim would happen actually... wouldn't. Merging brawl and weaponry isn't a miracle cure for your woes - its snake oil.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The CofD is a designed to encourage tropes that aren't not always optimal tactics. </div> </div> </div> ..... Even if that was true, that's not one that supports your arguments. CofD supports horror tropes, and you're not arguing for the sake of horror tropes. You're arguing for the sake of freeform combat where you can do anything with a single skill, which is completely different matter and one that the game does not support.<br /> <br /> What the design does support? Characters who aren't perfect. Characters with flaws and weaknesses and who trip and fail in the process. Having a universal skill for combat actually goes against this design principle, not support it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-06-2017, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T05:17:47-08:00","id":1044449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1044214#post1044214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Drawing a strong line.&quot; on a moral issue is meaningless if the game makes this choice mechanically superior. In the RAW, this choice has no really narrative power to it, because they take Brawl and related Merits, and ignore Weaponry. There's no <b>temptation</b> to pick up a weapon, because mechanically it's stupid for them to. In the game, instead of, &quot;I choose to take the harder path on moral grounds,&quot; it's, &quot;I'm going Brawl, so my best choice is to go 100% Brawl, so the choice to not use weapons is always mechanically superior for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> With a unified &quot;Melee,&quot; these guys are making a real choice in the system. With Brawl and Weaponry, it's not a moral choice, it's just a descriptive choice.<br /> <br /> If a character should roll Integrity as a Breaking Point for using a weapon instead of their fists (since that's probably more where this would come up over Aspirations/Anchors), and dumps all their combat stuff into Brawl and then never has a reason to face that Breaking point. If they take &quot;Melee&quot; every weapon around them is temptation to risk that Breaking Point. Every time combat is starting to go against them, they're making a meaningful choice to stick to their convictions, or compromise to win.<br /> <br /> That's what I want out of CofD games. Meaningful character decisions. Not just fluffed up reasons to have Brawl 5/Weaponry 0.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where you are coming from here, but... isn't that more a question of Role Playing? I mean, if I was a boxer with a mean hook, foregoing punching to grab a vase or soemthing to hit someone with it is a similar situation:The chances of success are, actually, lesser than if I went with something tried and true, namely punching him in the face. Many people that learned some sort of Martial Art are more likely to fall back on what they learned rather than use an unfamiliar weapon, be it a crowbar or a knife.<br /> The decision to forego my advantage to act appropriately scared/angry/headless etc. should be made by the player, and what is right for one troupe wouldn't work with another. That's a case by case thing.<br /> A Weponry 5/Brawl 0 PC can still make this choice and try to punch his way out, and a Brawl 5/ Weaponry 0 player can still decide to go for a weapon because his PC is appropriately freaked out: both roleplay well, and make a meaningful character decision (it's not like taking the moral high grounds is always the harder or better choice).<br /> <br /> At least, that is my take on it.<br /> <br /> And in regards to <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1044214#post1044214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is essentially a circular argument that comes down to, &quot;The system models it this way, so that's how it should be modeled.&quot;<br /> <br /> The system doesn't care about &quot;realistic&quot; XP investment. Science 5 is insanely broad competency for half the cost...</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't argue circularly, I gave my own opinion: &quot;My personal opinion is, this reflects the necessary training and focus well.&quot;<br /> You are welcome to disagree, as you obviously do, but in my experience, a person able to wield both weapons and their own body effectively is extremely uncommon, whereas someone that is very good with one and not very good at all with the other is less rare. I think the system models that well.<br /> <br /> Science is a whole different topic, and I agree that the competence gained per xp is insane. But see below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-06-2017, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T05:48:04-08:00","id":1044454,"title":"","content":"Design supports flaws...until you run into someone who wants to just be a singer or history buff. Singer somehow miraculously picks up ability to write speeches, paint, draw, write music, dance and so on, while History buff also becomes an expert on psychology, law, linguistics and tons of other fields. It's just jarring. System also doesn't support flawed characters, as it supports factotums who spread their dots all over the place - one-two dot purchases are more meaningful than investing 3-5 dots into something, especially with ability to Willpower the rolls in the picture. Creating character with some basic self defence capabilities is, currently, harder than becoming a Comic Books Style academics genius - especially at char gen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:14:55-08:00","id":1044485,"title":"","content":"Expression or Academics 1, appropiate specialty, field of expertise merit. There, Singer(History Buff right there.<br /> <br /> They wont be the best, but REALLY good. To be fair, even too good. I find it actually hard to belive for someone to be a complete master of any one field without a more hollistic and comprehensive education. Specially in ana Academic field. Music Conservatories teach stundents a wide range of instruments and msucial theory. Universities teach a whole range of courses. So if you want to be a &quot;Master&quot;, you will inevitably pick up a broader base of knowledge and practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:19:50-08:00","id":1044488,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> That I can understand, and yeah, if you allow &gt;3 dots at char gen, it get's quickly jarring. Most games I played in demanded a reasonable justification for why a char has 4 or 5 dots at the start of the game, + if you played e.g. a combat medic, you were required to have at least one dot in several things (Academics, Medicine, Science, Firearms, Brawl, Weaponry, Athletics, Survival) to reflect the training.<br /> <br /> Btw, I can achieve both a character with some <b>basic </b>self defence and a Comic Book style genius with 3, 4 dots. I agree, howver, that Expression, Academics and Science are rather catch-all.<br /> One Houserule I saw gave you a 'free' specialty in e.g. Science, but limited your rolls to that purview.<br /> However, I have a problem with that, too: A good chemist knows SOME physics (at least some thermodynamics and probably some electrodynamics) as well as a basic knowledge of biochemistry, thus neurology etc. It is also a lot easier to get into understanding e.g. pharmaceuticals (is that the right term? I feel like that is the right term). A geologist will likewise have some knowledge of chemistry, just as any biologist will have at least some working knowledge of chemistry. When it comes to applied work, then lab work in general has a lot of similarities, which closes the gap a bit.<br /> Thus, I think Science as a basic skill is alright, but definetely should have a specialty, and maybe a penalty to the science score when it comes to things not covered by the specialty. This would make buying specialties also a lot more tempting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:19:18-08:00","id":1044655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1044432#post1044432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm saying that your suggestions are unrealistic;</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering you keep misrepresenting what my suggestions would do, I find your statement of such rather baseless. You have made objectively false statements about how the rules work, and are accusing me of twisting the texts by pointing out what the text actually says. You continually assign absolutist or extreme motivations or thinking to me that I have not stated.<br /> <br /> So at this point, since you've demonstrated you don't actually care about what I'm really suggesting, what are you trying to say? Because right now I'm really not sure what you're trying to achieve other than bullying people that disagree with you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're arguing for the sake of freeform combat where you can do anything with a single skill, which is completely different matter and one that the game does not support. </div> </div> </div>Like this for example.<br /> <br /> Where have I advocated for freeform combat? Where I have advocated you can do anything in combat with a single Skill?<br /> <br /> Have I advocated for merging Firearms into this? Nope. I have advocated for removing Athletics from Defense, or throwing things? Nope.<br /> <br /> I have advocated for a single close-combat Skill, where all the other rules still apply as written. Combat is still rolled as is. Sure, some tweaks would need to be made regarding some of the Merits that rely on the separation of Brawl and Weaponry to no specify certain things. I have advocated for this change for reasons such as a character looking at an improvised weapon and considering the trade off in accuracy and initiative vs. the increase in possible damage and access to lethal damage (which matters a lot if you're struggling to inflict the Beaten Down tilt with bashing damage) without that being completely overridden by the Brawl/Weaponry divide.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Either actually engage with what I'm saying, or own up to whatever you're really trying to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1044449#post1044449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see where you are coming from here, but... isn't that more a question of Role Playing?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a RPG. The goal is for the game part to positively influence the role-playing part. The rules should inform and facilitate the RP you want to see happen with the game. In basic design principle, I reject the idea of mechanics that don't support the RP to be acceptable because you'll just RP over them. This is not an absolute thing, because design also requires compromise, and that is especially true when it comes to abstraction, but perfection not being the enemy of good, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons why I love the CofD 2e system compared to the 1e system or the WoD systems I played for so long, is because the designers did not let a lot of things slide in mechanical design that used to get a pass because &quot;Role Playing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, if I was a boxer with a mean hook, foregoing punching to grab a vase or soemthing to hit someone with it is a similar situation:The chances of success are, actually, lesser than if I went with something tried and true, namely punching him in the face. Many people that learned some sort of Martial Art are more likely to fall back on what they learned rather than use an unfamiliar weapon, be it a crowbar or a knife. </div> </div> </div>True. But that's why I was trying to bring up more dynamic scenarios than just, &quot;I'm better at punching&quot; in a white room. In a white room scenario you'll always do what you're best at.<br /> <br /> Your character gets jumped in an alley and the ambush does a few bashing. After a few rounds of people tossing tiny dice-pools or chance die, it's clear this is an even fight and that's bad for your PC because odds are you're going to get smacked with Beat Down first if it's just bashing damage flying around. But one success with a weapon is all you need to turn this fight around.<br /> <br /> Now there's a dramatic choice to make. Even more so if you have character traits that abhor weapon use. And that matters way more to me that separating out Brawl vs. Weaponry. To me, this sort of role-playing decision is better served by the broad Skill approach that is the default of the CofD system (seriously, the combat Skills are fairly narrow in comparison to pretty much everything else), rather than the more detailed combat systems that are currently in use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The decision to forego my advantage to act appropriately scared/angry/headless etc. should be made by the player, and what is right for one troupe wouldn't work with another. That's a case by case thing. </div> </div> </div>And backed up by things like Conditions and Tilts to help incentivize things mechanically. It's not just RP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't argue circularly, I gave my own opinion: &quot;My personal opinion is, this reflects the necessary training and focus well.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Circular reasoning and opinions aren't mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> As well, &quot;this reflects necessary training and focus well&quot; has to be in context of the system. Brawl 3/Weaponry 3 costs more than Science 5. So you're saying that being, say, a military close combat instructor that's really good at whatever it takes to defeat opponents in that context, costing more game investment than being one of the greatest polymaths of science that's mastered advanced understanding in dozens of fields is an appropriate reflection of the necessary training and focus.<br /> <br /> That doesn't come off a bit odd in context? Esp. given you're also posting about house rules to cut back on the broadness of Science given how much high levels of Science allow. But don't like Science... how about any other Skill? Socialize works to set up a rap battle as well as it works to set up a black tie fundraiser. Stealth covers moving silently as well as just blending in with crowds. The Skills in the game are generally very broad. Or how about this. Which Skills do you think are less broad than Brawl + Weaponry combined?<br /> <br /> This is how it's a bit circular in reasoning. Creation points/XP don't actually reflect necessary training or focus. It's a purely metagame resource, which some rules enforced social contract on how to spend it so that increases don't feel random. You can have Animal Ken 5 because you're a prodigy that just &quot;gets&quot; animals, or because you've spent decades studying animal behavior across dozens of species and learned how to interact with them through lots of hard work. The game doesn't care. It only reflects what you want it to reflect in this regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:37:28-08:00","id":1045004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1044655#post1044655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Circular reasoning and opinions aren't mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> As well, &quot;this reflects necessary training and focus well&quot; has to be in context of the system. Brawl 3/Weaponry 3 costs more than Science 5. So you're saying that being, say, a military close combat instructor that's really good at whatever it takes to defeat opponents in that context, costing more game investment than being one of the greatest polymaths of science that's mastered advanced understanding in dozens of fields is an appropriate reflection of the necessary training and focus.<br /> <br /> That doesn't come off a bit odd in context? Esp. given you're also posting about house rules to cut back on the broadness of Science given how much high levels of Science allow. But don't like Science... how about any other Skill? Socialize works to set up a rap battle as well as it works to set up a black tie fundraiser. Stealth covers moving silently as well as just blending in with crowds. The Skills in the game are generally very broad. Or how about this. Which Skills do you think are less broad than Brawl + Weaponry combined?<br /> <br /> This is how it's a bit circular in reasoning. Creation points/XP don't actually reflect necessary training or focus. It's a purely metagame resource, which some rules enforced social contract on how to spend it so that increases don't feel random. You can have Animal Ken 5 because you're a prodigy that just &quot;gets&quot; animals, or because you've spent decades studying animal behavior across dozens of species and learned how to interact with them through lots of hard work. The game doesn't care. It only reflects what you want it to reflect in this regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quoting the rest because I think we are more or less on the same page there, but simply have slightly different tastes.<br /> <br /> I think 6 xp is fair to express a combat instructor. That science or other skills are to broad from a competence/xp point of view is a different topic and I don't want to derail this thread too much.<br /> Let me put it like this: I think in many chronicles the physical fight gets more 'weight' than other systems, e.g. opening doors or chase etc., which is why a more narrow view there makes sense.<br /> If I was going to ST a game that had really little room for physical confrontation due to its theme or setup, but would delve a lot into mental/social stuff, I would probably houserule stuff and might introduce your proposed melee skill.<br /> <br /> thanks for that last part though, I can better understand where you're coming from or what you're trying to say, and partly, I'd agree. Maybe I just like the system the way it is since I am used to/comfortable with it. That's how grognards are born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:06:10-08:00","id":1045372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1007970-is-brawl-useless-for-mortals?p=1045004#post1045004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 6 xp is fair to express a combat instructor.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... 6 XP is what I'm asking for. You're saying that 12 XP is how much they should have (and that's not getting into Merits, or other Skills that would be appropriate for however someone gained their skills and their talent for training others). Brawl 3/Weaponry 3 is 12 XP total.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That science or other skills are to broad from a competence/xp point of view is a different topic and I don't want to derail this thread too much. </div> </div> </div>That's why I tried to move to <b>any</b> other Skill. I do think this remains relevant that Brawl and Weaponry (Brawl the most so) are very narrow is fundamental to the point of the thread. If Brawl did more (even if it wasn't in combat somehow), there wouldn't be complaints about how &quot;useless&quot; Brawl seems unless you're a supernatural with cheap access to Brawl enhancing powers (or at least some reason to invest a lot into Brawl. That's basically the fundamental issue. Brawl isn't actually worth the XP (at least for mortals) for what it does.<br /> <br /> Compare this to say, Brawl in Exalted 3e, where it's completely on par with Melee and Martial Arts (perhaps even better than Martial Arts for mortals since MA is expensive as it's balanced around what Exalts can do). There are different tactics you're going to want to focus on, but even without playing Exalts the Brawl focused character isn't going to feel the chump for not investing in Melee. Though Exalted 3e does have improvised weapons fall under both Brawl and Melee, and the difference between Bashing and Lethal damage is much smaller during a fight than in the CofD.<br /> <br /> The broadness issue is essential to the problem at hand.<br /> <br /> Though I'm thinking we're pretty tapped out on where to go with discussing it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T00:25:48-08:00","id":1045640,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for some reason I mixed up a few trains of thought there. I meant to say 6 xp is fair for a self defense trainer, 12 xp for a more diverse Martial Arts trainer seems appropriate, and a combat instructor should have about 3 Firearms, 2-3 Weaponry and 2-3 Brawl imo, so between 14 and 18 xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}